        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-amanda-d71a97b6aba54344a633abc8a978d5f7",
        "model": "GPT-6.1",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The current day 6 block specifies a private boat and car and a distinct historical account. Word p0039 describes a ferry instead and p0019 gives a different account, so no single compatible passage preserves the current transport basis and copy."
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, travel to Paraty in two stages, first by private boat and then by car. Check in at your hotel on arrival.\n\nParaty is about 125 miles from Rio and is known for its well-preserved eighteenth-century Portuguese colonial buildings. In the late 1700s, gold from the state of Minas Gerais was carried over the mountains to Paraty and shipped from there to Portugal.\n\nA more convenient route through Rio eventually took over, helping Paraty retain its historic buildings. The town later became a resort that draws visitors for its colonial architecture, beaches and coastal scenery."
    },
